      grammarNote: "-아도/-어도 表示\"即使……也……\"，前面接动词/形容词词干，表达让步关系。这里 \"잠기다（嘶哑）+ 어도\" 构成\"即使嗓子哑了\"的让步条件，后文用 \"-지 않는다\" 否定形式表达\"不停止\"。这是韩语中非常高频的基础句型。", grammarNoteEn: '-아도/-어도 means "even if..." and attaches to verb/adjective stems to express concession. Here, "잠기다 (hoarse) + 어도" forms the concessive condition "even if my voice is hoarse," and the following "-지 않는다" negative form expresses "doesn\'t stop." This is a very common basic pattern in Korean.',
