      zh: "绅士化具有双重性——与其说是物理环境的改善，不如说它伴随着对原住民的排斥。", zhEn: 'Gentrification is double-edged—rather than just physical improvement, it comes with the displacement of original residents.',
      grammarNote: "「-다기보다는」表示\"与其说A，不如说B\"，用于对两种描述进行对比取舍，语气客观且带有分析性，是C1书面语中常见的逻辑推进结构。本句同时使用了「-을 수반한다」（伴随）和「이중성을 지닌다」（具有双重性），体现了学术报道文体的精炼表达。", grammarNoteEn: '\'-다기보다는\' means \'rather than A, it\'s B,\' used to compare and choose between two descriptions. It carries an objective, analytical tone and is a common logical progression structure in C1 written language. This sentence also uses \'-을 수반한다\' (entails) and \'이중성을 지닌다\' (has a dual nature), reflecting the concise expression of academic report style.',
