        zh: "对移民第一代而言，母语既不是选择的对象，也不是需要刻意守护的遗产，而只是像呼吸一样在身体里流淌的什么。", zhEn: 'For the first generation of immigrants, the mother tongue is neither a matter of choice nor a heritage to be deliberately preserved—it\'s simply something that flows through the body like breathing.',
