      hint: "如果想不到身边的人，也可以写文学或电影中的人物。关键不是泛泛而谈'身份认同'，而是找到一个具体的物品或感官瞬间（一道菜的味道、一个动作的习惯、一种光线的颜色），让读者通过这个瞬间看到那个人与故乡的关系。用韩语写作时注意使用'-ㄴ다/는다'叙述体。", hintEn: 'If you can\'t think of someone close to you, you can also write about a character from literature or film. The key isn\'t to talk vaguely about \'identity,\' but to find a specific object or sensory moment (the taste of a dish, a habitual gesture, the color of a certain light) that lets the reader see that person\'s relationship with their hometown through that moment. When writing in Korean, remember to use the \'-ㄴ다/는다\' narrative style.',
